# FoxML_Trader_v2 house style is HAND-LAID — branchless/SIMD kernels with
# deliberate column alignment, hand-wrapped comments, and the "preserve the
# user's voice in comments" discipline (CLAUDE.md). clang-format's default
# style fights all of that (it reflowed FixedPointN.hpp on a plugin save,
# 2026-07-01).
#
# So: disable clang-format ENTIRELY on this repo. Any format-on-save path
# (clangd LSP textDocument/formatting, conform.nvim, null-ls, vim.lsp.buf.format)
# reads this file and becomes a NO-OP — it must never reflow the hand-alignment.
# fox-symdeps.nvim (navigation/symbol-deps, clangd-backed) is unaffected; it
# does not format. If a future need arises to auto-format NEW code, craft a
# house-matching config then — do not enable a default style repo-wide.
DisableFormat: true
SortIncludes: false
